| Spaces around signs of comparison (Add spaces)
| To add spaces selectively around signs of comparison in math within .txx
| Note that all characters are as encoded in DUSCI & so should agree with .bts
|  1;1  2014-03-23/24/jes
|  1;2  2014-03-25/jes: Allow [bar] to preserve state 3 (see ex0006)| States:
|  1;3  2015-01-12/cln: Handle signs of comparison after [ts], [l], and [<]
|     and before [te] and [l] and [<].
|     When adding space before a comparison sign, insert [big] before the space.
|     Run a companion scrub table next to deal with the [big] followed by space.
|     After [ts], [l], and [<] the [big] and space will be removed.
|     Elsewhere only the [big] will be removed.
|  1;4  2015-06-15/jes: Add U+221d Proportional to {"varies as"}} (DUSCI |240M)
|     as sign of comparison (following same patterns as
|     U+223c Tilde operator (DUSCI |240l);
|     use clnbts to ensure coding consistent with .bts
|  1;5  2015-12-06/jes: Allow space addition next to codes generally (not just
|     [fs] etc. as in previous version), with amspcob.sbt now doing more
|     cleanup (e.g. when [te] is followed by a space), so that the pattern for
|     space addition is much simpler and overall more spaces are added;
|     provide that [ts] & [te] codes with associated "idle" codes indicating
|     text within math ("embedded" text) are passed through transparently
|  1;7  2017-07-17/jes: Add support for
|     D%|221|164 U+2af4 Triple vertical bar binary relation
|     D%|221|165 U+2af5 Triple vertical bar with horizontal stroke
|  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
|  States:
|   1 outside [ts]...[te], i.e. not in math
|   (other states are all within [ts]...[te], i.e. in math:)
|   2 at baseline just after a code (with some exceptions) or space or
|     otherwise NOT READY to add space to coming symbol
|   3 at baseline just after nonspace symbol or exceptional code or
|     otherwise READY to add space to coming symbol if appropriate
|     36  2 |240:~^e~ {U+220a Small element of}
|     |2402 - partial differential
|     |240x - almost equal to
|   4 at baseline just after DUSCI prefix
|   5 at baseline just after beginning of code (|028)
|   6 at baseline inside code
|   7 not at baseline
|  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
